CATEGORIES:community
DESCRIPTION:https://sf.funcheap.com/love-birds-awardwinning-doc-postfilm-q
 a-roxie-theater/\nLocation: san francisco\nCategories: community\nSource: 
 funcheap/san-francisco\n\nLove Birds\, an award-winning documentary short 
 directed by Elliott Kennerson and Angel Morris\, tells the remarkable stor
 y of the female gull pairs found on California’s Santa Barbara Island in
  1972 and the personal and political fallout of the discovery. This specta
 cular film returns to San Francisco on November 19 for a screening at the 
 Roxie Theater\, with a post-screening Q&A with filmmaker Elliott Kennerson
  and moderator Judy Irving. Preceded by a program of short documentary off
 icial selections from the International Ocean Film Foundation (IOFF). Prog
 ram: Birdathlon \, Karen Lewis (USA) 4 min How do Pelicans Survive Their D
 eath-Defying Dives \, Elliott Kennerson\, (USA) 4 min The Wild Parrots of 
 Telegrapn Hill “Sneak Peek” \, Judy Irving (USA) 20 min Love Birds \, 
 Elliott Kennerson\, (USA) 28 min
LOCATION:san francisco
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/love-birds-awardwinning-doc-postfilm-qa-roxie-
 theater/
END:VEVENT
