SUMMARY:[Bay/Free] Free Winter Art Exhibition: “What We Carry” (Dec. 3
 -Feb. 14)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T210000
DTSTAMP:20261118T235101Z
UID:funcheap-20261203-freewinterartexhibitionw
CATEGORIES:community,free
DESCRIPTION:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-winter-art-exhibition-carry-dec-3
 feb-14/\nLocation: san francisco\nPrice: Free\nCategories: community\, fre
 e\nSource: funcheap/san-francisco\n\nAl-An deSouza\, Angela Hennessy\, Ste
 phanie Syjuco\, Rupy C. Tut\, and Maryam Yousif December 3\, 2026–Februa
 ry 14\, 2027 Thacher Gallery\, University of San Francisco Five Bay Area a
 rtists explore questions of inheritance from those who came before us–in
  our bodies\, in our materials\, and in our shared record–and what we ma
 ke of what we choose to keep. Presented by the MA in Museum Studies progra
 m in collaboration with guest curator and instructor Deena Chalabi. What W
 e Carry is on view in Thacher Gallery from. Closed Dec. 19-20\, and Dec. 2
 4-Jan. 3. Located in USF’s Gleeson Library-Geschke Center\, the Thacher 
 Gallery is free and open to the public from noon to 6 pm daily at 2130 Ful
 ton Street. usfca.edu/thacher-gallery Holiday hours. Image: Rupy C. Tut\, 
 (detail) Beeji da Ghar (My Grandmother’s Home)\, 2023 (Photo by Phillip 
 Maisel)
LOCATION:san francisco
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-winter-art-exhibition-carry-dec-3feb-14/
